> We had a good session, with Austin's character Ekemon reaching level 3. The next adventure I want to be focused on getting to Redclaw Cliffs, with the hope of getting an NPC Dragonborn to help him on his campaign-long quest to become a Titan. He has a Titan Seed, from the temple he raided, which beats like a heart.
> 
> I said before that Redclaw Cliffs was a human town near where red dragons dwelt, so that would be a reasonable place to find dragonborn.
> 
> For this adventure, Ekemon (tiefling) is on his own again, but he has a fair amount of money and he also want to get a club for another weapon.
**assistant**:
> Nice, go Ekemon! Level 3 is perfect timing for “get a cool ally and a new weapon” energy.
> 
> Here’s a 1‑session adventure scaffold to get him to Redclaw Cliffs, introduce dragonborn, and tee up a long‑term dragonborn companion, with simple choices and kid‑friendly tension.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Big Picture
> 
> **Goal of the session:**
> - Travel to **Redclaw Cliffs**.
> - Let Ekemon:
>   - Buy a **club**.
>   - Notice/meet **dragonborn** (especially one potential companion).
>   - Do one clear **adventure challenge** (combat + small story choice).
> - End with: a strong hook into a **future “arena/auction” style scene** where he can *win or earn* a dragonborn champion.
> 
> Assuming ~1 hour, we’ll do:
> 
> 1. Short travel → one encounter on the way.  
> 2. Arrival at Redclaw Cliffs → first impressions.  
> 3. Quick town segment: buy club, see dragon stuff, meet key NPC.  
> 4. End on a strong “cliffhanger” or clear next step.
> 
> You can compress or expand each step as needed.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 1. Getting to Redclaw Cliffs
> 
> Start with a quick reminder:
> 
> > “Ekemon, the temple behind you is quiet now. In your pack, the **Titan Seed** thumps like a tiny heart: thump… thump… thump… reminding you that you’re meant to become a Titan. Ahead, smoke rises from the **Redclaw Cliffs**, a town built high on red rocks, near the lairs of red dragons.”
> 
> Ask a simple choice to get him engaged:
> 
> - “Do you walk boldly on the road,”  
> - “or sneak along the edges and shadows?”
> 
> Either way, give him a short, fun **travel encounter** that shows the Seed is special and gives a little combat.
> 
> ### Encounter on the Road: The Greedy Rock-Lizard
> 
> **Setup:**  
> He passes under steep rocks. The Titan Seed pulses faster. Suddenly, a **red-scaled drake-like lizard** (CR ~1; just reskin a **giant lizard** or **guard drake** with fire flavor) drops down from the rocks.
> 
> It sniffs and speaks broken Common:
> 
> > “Smell… power… in your bag. Give shiny heart-stone to Redfang, or I bite!”
> 
> Offer him a clear choice:
> 1. Fight the Rock-Lizard.
> 2. Try to scare/intimidate it.
> 3. Trick it or bargain (“You can’t have this one, but I’ll give you coins/junk weapon instead.”)
> 
> Mechanical simplification:
> - AC 13–14, HP ~22.
> - Bite: +4 to hit, 1d8+2 damage.
> - Optional “fiery spit” 1/day: 10‑ft line, Dex save, 1d6 fire.
> 
> Give the Seed a little flavor effect:
> - If he draws close to kill the lizard, the Seed **thumps faster**, and he feels a surge of power (you could grant:
>   - +1 to hit on one attack, or
>   - temporary 3 HP, or
>   - advantage on one roll this fight).
> 
> Make it clear this is the **Titan Seed reacting to danger**, not just random.
> 
> If he tries **not** to fight, let that work too:
> - Intimidation: lizard backs off, muttering, “Redclaw town smell like dragons. They will want the heart-stone too…”
> - Trickery: It grabs the decoy and runs, but drops something: a **melted red scale** or **small dragon-shaped charm** he can later show in town.
> 
> Reward:  
> - A few coins or a little loot from its nest in a nearby hollow (you can say he spots the nest afterwards).
> - More importantly: **foreshadowing** that dragons and dragonborn will be interested in the Seed.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 2. First Look at Redclaw Cliffs
> 
> Describe the town visually and simply:
> 
> > “At last, you see **Redclaw Cliffs**. Houses and towers cling to the side of a huge red rock cliff. Ramps and stairs wind upward. Smoke rises from forges. Flags show a red dragon claw on a black field.”
> >
> > “You see **people**… and also **dragonborn**: tall, dragon‑like people with scales, horns, and tails. Some red, some brass, some bronze. You can smell hot metal and spicy food.”
> 
> Give him a small decision:
> 
> - Go first to the **market** (to get his club).  
> - Or go to the **noisy arena square**, where he hears cheering and roaring.
> 
> Whichever he chooses first, you can still show both, but the choice lets him feel in control.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 3. The Market: Buying the Club
> 
> At the **market**, have a simple blacksmith or weapon-seller.
> 
> ### NPC: Brona Ironjaw (Human Blacksmith)
> - Big arms, soot-stained face, warm but a little wary of tieflings.
> - Speaks plainly: “You buying or just staring, horn-boy?”
> 
> Have her display a few simple things on the counter:
> - A regular **club** (1 gp or less; maybe even free as a “thug special”).  
> - A **spiky club** (same stats, just cooler flavor).  
> - Optional: a **weird little trident** or whip upgrade, just to remind him of his signature weapons.
> 
> Offer **two or three choices**, tops:
> - “You can get a **plain heavy club**, a **spiky mean club**, or a **big wooden mallet** that bonks really hard but looks silly. Which one do you want?”
> 
> Let the Titan Seed react briefly:
> - When he touches weapons, it beats once powerfully, like it’s “approving” of power.
> 
> Optional hook:
> - Brona glances at the Seed bulge in his bag if it shifts:
>   - “Whatever that is in your pack, don’t wave it around in Redclaw. Some dragonborn around here like power a little too much.”
> 
> This line foreshadows the dragonborn who might want to own/use him—or at least the Seed.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 4. The Arena Square: Dragonborn and a Future Companion
> 
> Move him to or from the **arena square**:
> 
> > “You come to a big open square cut into the cliff. There’s a raised stone platform like a stage or fighting ring. Crowds are gathered, cheering. On one side, a human announcer shouts. On the other, a tall, chained **red dragonborn** warrior stands with crossed arms.”
> 
> You don’t need to do the full auction/contract scene yet; just **introduce** the world and one special dragonborn.
> 
> ### NPC: Varkash Redscale (Potential Companion)
> - Red dragonborn gladiator.
> - Muscular, scar over one eye.
> - Looks proud, not broken.
> - Has simple manacles / a heavy collar: “bound champion” visual, but keep it light.
> 
> Announcer (or a crier on a crate) is shouting something like:
> 
> > “Step right up! Champions fight for glory and contracts! Need a bodyguard? Need a gladiator to win you prizes? Sign a **fighting contract** and a champion is yours—for gold, glory, and a piece of the winnings!”
> 
> Emphasize: this is like **sports+contract**, not slavery.
> 
> #### First Contact Moment
> 
> Let Ekemon catch Varkash’s eye:
> 
> > Varkash’s nostrils flare. He sniffs the air, then stares straight at your backpack.
> >
> > “You, tiefling. That heartbeat… you carry something powerful.”
> 
> Give Ekemon a choice:
> 1. Go up and **talk to Varkash**.  
> 2. Ignore him and **watch a short fight**.  
> 3. Talk to the **announcer/manager** instead.
> 
> You can keep things very short.
> 
> ##### If he talks to Varkash
> 
> Varkash, quietly:
> 
> > “My name is **Varkash Redscale**. I fight in this pit for prize money and to pay off my ‘contract.’”
> >
> > “I can smell dragonfire and something older, beating like a heart. You have something inside your pack, don’t you?”
> >
> > “Be careful, little villain. People here will try to use you—or what you carry.”
> 
> He can hint:
> - “If you ever need a **dragonborn champion**, win a match or win enough gold, and I could fight by your side… instead of for these fools.”
> 
> This plants him as the **future companion**, but doesn’t force the moment now.
> 
> ##### If he watches a short fight
> 
> Keep it very fast, almost like a cutscene:
> - Varkash vs. a simple human or orc fighter.
> - Narrate a couple of blows and Varkash’s flashy, dragon‑breath‑y move.
> - He wins, crowd cheers.
> 
> Then Varkash looks up at Ekemon and says something like:
> > “One day, I’d rather fight beside you than in front of them.”
> 
> Again, just a seed.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 5. One Small Challenge in Town (Optional but Recommended)
> 
> If you have time and he’s still engaged, give him one **local problem** that:
> - Lets him use his **new club**.
> - Shows dragonborn society.
> - Can be resolved quickly.
> 
> ### Quick Hook: Fire Imp in the Forges
> 
> A blacksmith (maybe Brona) runs up to him:
> 
> > “You! Horned kid with too many weapons! A flaming little creature is loose in my forge! If it melts my tools, I’ll be ruined. I’ll pay you to smack it out!”
> 
> Introduce a tiny **fire imp/salamander**:
> - Think of it as an **Imp** or **Magma Mephit**, simplified:
>   - AC ~12, HP ~14, claw attack 1d6+2 fire.
>   - Maybe a 1/day “puff of flame” for 1d4 fire in close range.
> 
> This is a short, contained **combat in town** that:
> - Feels important.
> - Gives a small gold reward or a **discount on the club** / future gear.
> - Lets the Titan Seed thump with excitement near fire.
> 
> Possible Seed moment:
> - When the imp blasts fire, the Seed **absorbs some**; maybe Ekemon takes 1 less fire damage once.
>   - You can say: “You feel the Seed drink in the fire. It likes dangerous power.”
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 6. Ending the Session
> 
> Wrap with a clear *next step* and a satisfying “I did stuff” feeling.
> 
> Options for an ending line:
> 
> 1. **Arena hook ending:**
>    > “As the sun sets over Redclaw Cliffs, the arena torches flare to life. A poster is nailed up:  
>    > ‘**Tomorrow: Free Challenge Fights! Win a Champion Contract!**’  
>    > Varkash catches your eye and nods.  
>    > The Titan Seed in your bag beats faster. Thump… thump… thump…”
> 
> 2. **Dragonborn intrigue ending:**
>    > “As you walk back through the market, a cloaked **bronze dragonborn** bumps into you.  
>    > ‘Careful,’ she whispers. ‘Some here want to take that heart‑stone from you.’  
>    > When you look up, she’s already vanished into the crowd. The Seed keeps beating…”
> 
> 3. **Rest-and-prepare ending:**
>    > “You find a cheap inn built into the rock. As you lie in your bed, you can hear distant dragon roars from the cliffs above and cheering from the arena below.  
>    > The Titan Seed beats like a drum in the night. It feels like it’s waiting… for the next fight
