> Perfect. Let’s lean into that and make it feel big, clear, and still kid‑friendly.
> 
> Below is a **runnable outline** for this next scene: Ekemon tries to buy Varkash’s contract, discovers it’s expensive, and gets a concrete short quest (or challenge fight) to earn it.
> 
> You can do this all in one session, or spread over two if needed.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 1. Opening: Ekemon States His Goal
> 
> Remind him of where you left off (arena square, etc.) and then let him say it.
> 
> > DM: “You stand by the arena in Redclaw Cliffs. The red dragonborn champion, **Varkash Redscale**, wipes sweat from his snout after another victory.  
> > The crowd shouts, coins fly, and the Titan Seed in your pack beats: thump… thump… thump…  
> > What do you want to do?”
> >
> > Player: “I want to pay for his contract!”
> 
> Acknowledge it in‑world:
> 
> > Varkash hears you and grins, showing sharp teeth. “You want me to fight for *you*, little Titan? Then we must talk to my handler.”
> 
> He waves over the arena manager.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 2. Meet the Contract Holder
> 
> ### NPC: Korga the Contract-Keeper
> - Race: Human or half‑orc.
> - Personality: Slick but not too evil; more like a greedy sports agent.
> - Visual: Tall, fancy coat with lots of pockets, scroll‑tubes hanging from his belt with contracts.
> 
> Korga walks up, looking Ekemon over.
> 
> > Korga: “So, the little tiefling wants a **dragonborn champion**. Interesting.”  
> > “Varkash has a **fighting contract**. That means whoever pays the cost gets his strength on their side… for a while.”
> 
> Frame it like a **sports contract**, not slavery:
> 
> > Korga: “He isn’t a slave. He’s a **bound champion**. You pay the gold, he fights for *you*, and you share the prizes. Fair deal.”
> 
> ---
> 
> ## 3. The Price (Too High… at First)
> 
> Ask how much gold Ekemon has, but don’t make him do much math. You mainly want him to realize:
> 
> - The contract costs **more gold than he has now**,  
> - But there’s a way to **earn it** by doing something cool.
> 
> You can say:
> 
> > Korga: “To buy his contract fully? That would be… 200 gold pieces.”  
> > (Make it clearly bigger than whatever Ekemon has.)
> 
> Let Ekemon respond. If he says “I don’t have that much!” give him options immediately.
> 
> > Korga (thinking): “Hmm. You *do* look dangerous, and the crowd likes you.”  
> > “We could make a **deal**.”
> >
> > “You have two ways to earn a **dragonborn champion contract**:  
> > 1. **Win a special fight** in the arena and impress the sponsors.  
> > 2. **Do a job for me** outside the arena that brings me profit.”  
> 
> Then ask Ekemon:
> 
> > “Do you want to try a **special fight**, or go on a **job/quest** for Korga?”
> 
> Either option ends with Varkash’s contract coming to him, so you can steer toward whichever seems more fun for Austin.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## OPTION A: The Arena Challenge Fight
> 
> If he chooses the fight:
> 
> > Korga: “Very well. One **Free Challenge Fight**. Win, and I cut the price down so low it’s like you paid in glory instead of gold. Lose… and we talk about that job instead.”
> 
> Describe the arena:
> 
> > “You step into the stone ring. The crowd roars. Varkash stands on the side, arms crossed, watching you.  
> > The Titan Seed in your bag is pounding with excitement: thump‑thump‑thump.”
> 
> ### Opponent: “Flame-Fist Rokan”
> 
> - Race: Human or half‑orc brawler. CR around 1–2, keep it simple.
> - AC: 13–14, HP: ~26.
> - Attacks: Two unarmed strikes per round (or one big hit), 1d6+2 each.
> - Special: Once per fight he can do a “Flame Fist”:
>   - The crowd chants, he dips his fists into brazier coals, gets advantage on one attack and adds +1d6 fire damage.
> 
> Make the fight dynamic but quick. Also give Ekemon **one little Titan Seed boost**:
> 
> > At a tense moment, say: “You feel the Titan Seed’s heartbeat speed up. If you want, it can give you a **burst of strength** this turn: you get advantage on one attack roll or gain 5 temporary HP.”  
> > (Let him pick one.)
> 
> Have Varkash shout advice:
> 
> > “Use your new club! Go low, sweep his legs!”  
> > “Don’t let him corner you by the wall!”
> 
> When Ekemon wins:
> 
> > The crowd explodes in cheers. Korga grins.  
> > “Well, well. The people like you. A deal’s a deal.”  
> > He pulls out a scroll and slashes a big line through it.  
> > “Varkash Redscale’s contract is **now bound to you**, Ekemon the Titan‑Seeker.”
> 
> Have Varkash kneel or bow a bit:
> 
> > “From this day, I fight for you. Not as a slave, but as your **sworn champion**. Until our contract is over… or until you are a Titan, if you dare keep me that long.”
> 
> Ekemon now has his **dragonborn companion**.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## OPTION B: The Job/Quest for the Contract
> 
> If he chooses the job instead of a fight (or loses the fight and Korga offers another path):
> 
> > Korga: “I like your style. There’s a **problem** in Redclaw Cliffs, and fixing it will be worth more than gold to me.”
> 
> Give him a **small, one-session quest**. A few kid‑friendly options:
> 
> ### Quest Hook 1: The Stolen Prize Chest
> 
> > “Someone stole a **chest of prize money** from beneath the arena. I think it’s hidden in the old tunnels under the cliffs.  
> > Bring it back, and I’ll sign Varkash over to you.”
> 
> The adventure:
> - Simple mini‑dungeon: 2–3 rooms/tunnels.
> - Enemies: a few bandits or sneaky goblins who grabbed the chest.
> - One minor environmental challenge (a rickety bridge, a crumbling ledge).
> - At the end, the chest (maybe partly looted).
> 
> When he returns it, even if some coins are gone:
> 
> > Korga: “Good enough. A deal’s a deal. Varkash is yours.”
> 
> ### Quest Hook 2: The Loose Fire Beast
> 
> > “A **fire lizard / young fire drake** broke free from its cage and fled into the lower town. If it burns someone’s shop, I pay. I don’t like paying.  
> > Knock it out or chase it away, and I’ll count it as payment for the contract.”
> 
> Short urban hunt:
> - Track some scorch marks.
> - Fight/drive off one fiery creature (similar stats to your road lizard).
> - Maybe give the Seed a cool moment absorbing fire.
> 
> Return to Korga, get contract, same “Varkash is yours” scene.
> 
